[=[return {c={"How it works"},e={{"r","+ Add Smart Macro",1,0,0},{"r","+ Add Bar Slot",1,0,0},{"c","How it works",1,1,0},{"d","How it works",1,1,0,"1. Create an empty macro in WoW's Macro UI and give it any name (e.g. SmartBomb)."},{"r","2. Add a Smart Macro here using that exact name, then add Rules.",1,1,0},{"d","2. Add a Smart Macro here using that exact name, then add Rules.",1,1,0,"3. Rules are checked top-to-bottom on every target change. The first rule whose condition matches AND whose required item (if set) is in your bags and off cooldown is applied."},{"d","2. Add a Smart Macro here using that exact name, then add Rules.",1,1,0,"4. If no rule fires, the macro keeps its last-written body (sticky). A rule with an empty body clears (blanks) the macro when it fires."},{"d","2. Add a Smart Macro here using that exact name, then add Rules.",1,1,0,"5. IN COMBAT THE MACRO CANNOT CHANGE. Blizzard blocks macro edits during combat, so a swap you trigger mid-fight is queued and applied the moment you drop combat. Target your next mob before the pull to get the right body."},{"d","2. Add a Smart Macro here using that exact name, then add Rules.",1,1,0,"6. Use 'Active in' to scope a macro to one raid (and optionally one raid profile). To make the SAME in-game macro do different things per raid config, add several Smart Macros with the same name, each scoped to a different raid/profile."},{"d","2. Add a Smart Macro here using that exact name, then add Rules.",1,1,0,"7. ONE ITEM FOR A BOSS OR A ROUTE STEP. A boss's page in Raid Config (the Macros tile) and a route step (Add action) can hand a macro one item: while that boss is your target, or the route is on that step, the macro uses it whatever its rules say. Give macros the same Group and one line swaps them all - every potion key becomes the same potion. When the boss or step is over the rules decide again, and a macro with no matching rule gets back the text it had."},{"d","2. Add a Smart Macro here using that exact name, then add Rules.",1,1,0,"8. ONLY ON BOSSES WHERE IT IS SWITCHED ON. Under an ability on a boss's page (Death Wish, Recklessness, Potion...) link the buttons that use it - click them in the preview of your bars, or tick Automatic and they are found for you. A linked button gets a small macro in place of its spell or item (same key, same icon); nothing is taken off your bars. On a boss that is set up but has the ability off, that macro does nothing; on a boss with nothing set up, and everywhere else, the key is as you made it. A key linked to Potion or Utility uses the boss's item where the boss has exactly one set up."},{"d","2. Add a Smart Macro here using that exact name, then add Rules.",1,1,0,"9. BAR SLOTS. '+ Add Bar Slot' adds one slot of your action bars instead of a macro, for a group: a boss's page or a route step can hand the slot - or its whole group - one item. Pick it by clicking its button, in the preview of your bars or on the bars themselves. It works with any bar addon; what the slot held is put back afterwards, and a slot is never emptied."},{"d","2. Add a Smart Macro here using that exact name, then add Rules.",1,1,0,"10. WAIT. A key linked to a boss ability cannot be locked until the ability's reminder goes off - the game lets no addon change a macro or a bar slot in a fight. Its button on your bars is dimmed and reads WAIT on the boss instead, until the reminder has gone off."},{"d","2. Add a Smart Macro here using that exact name, then add Rules.",1,1,0,"Tip: Use 'Required item' to handle shared cooldowns. Example: Name 'Crypt Stalker' + Req. item 'Goblin Sapper Charge' fires only when the sapper is available. When the sapper is on CD the rule is skipped and the next rule (Undead -> Holy Water) fires instead."}},f={},p={},t={""}}]=],
